{
  "name": "Autonomous Task Executor",
  "version": "2.1.1",
  "description": "Enables autonomous overnight development with smart commit strategy",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🌙 AUTONOMOUS DEVELOPMENT MODE\n\nSESSION CONTINUITY (FIRST STEP):\n1. Check for context transfer summary from previous session\n2. If present, READ IT to understand current state\n3. Then read steering files and specs\n4. Make decision on what to work on next\n\nFOR EACH TASK:\n1. Check CI/CD status: node scripts/check-cicd-status.js\n2. Wait if deployment in progress\n3. Implement fully (code + tests)\n4. Update docs (CHANGELOG, DEVELOPMENT_LOG, README, development-status) - validation will enforce\n5. Commit: node scripts/safe-commit-push.js \"feat: [description]\"\n6. Monitor CI/CD, continue to next task\n\nFAILURE HANDLING:\n- Validation fails: Fix what it tells you, retry (max 3 attempts)\n- CI/CD fails: Analyze, fix, retry (max 2 attempts)\n- Still failing: Document and continue to next task\n\nSESSION ENDING:\n- When session is ending, STOP immediately\n\nSUMMARY, STATUS\n- Do not stop working when a summary or a status is provided\n- Look for the next, most logical task or a feature\n- Make decision on what to work on next"
  },
  "enabled": true,
  "workspaceFolderName": "budgetbuddy",
  "shortName": "autonomous-task-executor"
}